      <p>A documentation set is easier to fix when you can see it. The editor can describe how every map, topic, key, and DITAVAL file connects, and turn that, or any other check, into a standalone HTML page. The page is a single file that opens from disk in any browser, with no internet connection, so you can attach it to a ticket or keep it next to the content.</p>
      <h2 id="examples" class="group scroll-mt-20">Examples<a href="#examples" class="ml-2 text-muted-foreground opacity-0 group-hover:opacity-100 no-underline" aria-hidden="true" tabindex="-1" data-pagefind-ignore>&para;</a></h2>
      <p>These pages were generated from the <a href="https://github.com/dogsbay/dogsbay-xml-dita-tutorial">DITA tutorial project</a>, which has problems planted in it on purpose. Each is the single file the command writes, published as it is.</p>
      <ul>
